    "done_when": "Three parts, in order. (1) imas_ambix/data/selene_deck.py build_pf_active names each pf_active/coil/element entry, which is one of the SELENE deck's rectangular current filaments of a coil (40 per CS module, 16 per EF coil, 6 per FPPC coil, 268 across the 12 coils), after its coil and its 1-based position in that coil, for example CS1_1 to CS1_40 and EF1_1 to EF1_16; and selene_deck.py declares __all__ naming only write_phase_description and whatever any module under imas_ambix, scripts or tests imports from it, so its public surface is the one converter entry point the plan states, and the existing every-entry-is-named test in tests/data/test_selene_deck.py is extended to the coil-element level, failing if any element is unnamed or a name repeats within its coil. Commit that change. (2) Re-convert OP1 and OP2 with write_phase_description from the committed code, reading only the sha256-verified copies in /work/projects/imas_gpu/jt60sa/machine_description/source/ (refuse on any sha256 that differs from /work/projects/imas_gpu/jt60sa/machine_description/source/provenance.json). Record the sha256 of every existing file in /work/projects/imas_gpu/jt60sa/machine_description/OP1/ and /work/projects/imas_gpu/jt60sa/machine_description/OP2/ before writing. Write each new file under a temporary name in the same directory and rename it into place, so a concurrent reader sees the old or the new file and never a partial one; a peer session's figure work reads this store. Read every file back through imas.DBEntry at DD 4.1.1: all 268 coil filaments are named, the coil and vessel-loop names and all counts are unchanged, and each receipt names the new converter commit. (3) In imas_ambix/data/machine_maps/jt-60sa.json, every pf_active structure assembly's element_identifiers take the store's element names in place of the placeholder identifiers that end in a slash; the file is edited line by line, never re-serialised whole. This session runs inside the fleet SLURM allocation (SLURM_JOB_ID is set), so the gate runs in place: TMPDIR=/tmp UV_PROJECT_ENVIRONMENT=/home/ITER/mcintos/Code/imas-ambix/.venv PYTHONPATH=$PWD command uv run --no-sync pytest -p no:cacheprovider -n 8 tests/data/test_selene_deck.py tests/data/test_jt60sa_machine_map.py tests/data/test_description_reader.py tests/data/test_description_identity.py tests/data/test_transform_engine.py > <your log> 2>&1; echo EXIT=$?, exiting 0, with the gate log's first line naming the revision, the tree and the command, and a test asserting that no element identifier in jt-60sa.json ends in a slash. UV_PROJECT_ENVIRONMENT=/home/ITER/mcintos/Code/imas-ambix/.venv PYTHONPATH=$PWD command uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests exits 0. The evidence fragment docs/evidence/fragments/jt60sa-machine-map/jtmm-coil-element-names.html lists per phase and file the replaced and new sha256, the element names read back for one coil of each size, and the converter commit. Nothing outside /work/projects/imas_gpu/jt60sa/machine_description/OP1 and /work/projects/imas_gpu/jt60sa/machine_description/OP2 is written under /work/projects/imas_gpu/jt60sa/machine_description, and the JT-60SA server is never contacted (no ssh jt-60sa, no EDDB call).",
    "estimated_hours": 2.0,
